{"overview":"Ralph Grey visits France with his shipbuilder father, and falls in love with Blossom, granddaughter of his father's friend, a Civil war veteran not reconciled with the Union. Blossom, however, is engaged to a French nobleman. When war breaks out, Ralph enlists, while his brother Jim, a heartbreaker, is drafted.","tagline":"D.W. Griffith's Vital Story of Today","cast":[{"n":"Adolph Lestina","c":"Mr. France","p":"/r7mwL8DBUy7A9MDgRejog9R2TPE.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Carol Dempster","c":"Atoline France","p":"/azSHQHijC9MLNw5e4HkA56PjgLY.jpg","q":"Q932255"},{"n":"Frances Parks","c":"The chum","p":"/3wnXh6TSSqX9zRf4UE4E2HFlfim.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Richard Barthelmess","c":"Ralph Grey","p":"/p7nmZeuQjHOsNFgqgEXBdh78OSC.jpg","q":"Q457293"},{"n":"Robert Harron","c":"James Grey","p":"/8uqveFAwItcd5Ty2OEMPM37bbZb.jpg","q":"Q1344716"},{"n":"Syn De Conde","c":"Count de Brissac","p":"/2QYlvFC2jG4HEqiahhXmD4zveKE.jpg","q":null},{"n":"George Fawcett","c":"Edward Grey","p":"/pZBmcj6XkdBkNKvUIovZMNqg8qU.jpg","q":"Q357552"},{"n":"Kate Bruce","c":"Mrs. Edward Grey","p":"/oLC99DsB0gkPdsZJRi0d1D1B4hD.jpg","q":"Q2461823"},{"n":"Edward Peil Sr.","c":"Turnverein Terror","p":"/tkebpmT8PggXYd2Qu028umqEZzc.jpg","q":null},{"n":"Clarine Seymour","c":"Cutie Beautiful","p":"/rSuByxezOUTHmogpt42GEGnLX84.jpg","q":"Q2185148"}],"country":["United States"],"language":[],"wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Girl_Who_Stayed_at_Home","qid":"Q7736541"}